From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: send frames redirected over XDP

On an AP interface with zero_touch set, mac80211 passes ath11k the
Ethernet frames another device redirected over XDP. Queue a run of them
on one TCL ring under one lock, look the station up once per
destination, take the TID from the DSCP, and write the head pointer on
XDP_XMIT_FLUSH. The completion counts each frame for its station and
returns the frames in bulk. Frames to unauthorized, TKIP or 4-address
stations, multicast and non-IP frames are refused and take the normal
path. The interface gets Ethernet encapsulation while zero_touch is set,
whatever the frame_mode.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
